<urn:atm:triage:finding/FNX-013>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FNX-013" ;
  triage:title "attention_opportunities retention prunes on the writer hot path instead of a maintenance tick" ;
  triage:description "fenix's re-verification pass on PR #1395 (head 3b8a43fd3) reports prune_terminal_rows(connection) runs unconditionally at the top of every reserve_writer call (attention_schedule_store.rs:246,331) -- before the same-opportunity idempotency short-circuit, so retries pay it too. It issues two DELETEs, the second sorting all terminal rows (ORDER BY created_at DESC, rowid DESC LIMIT -1 OFFSET 10000), and the only index on the table is (team, agent, roster_state_revision) -- neither status nor created_at is indexed. The comparator pattern (diagnostic_timeline) instead prunes from a bootstrap maintenance tick (diagnostic_timeline.rs:295), never from the write path. Impact is low since ATTENTION_MAX_TERMINAL_ROWS bounds the scanned set at ~10k, self-limiting the cost -- which is why this is minor. Recommendation: call prune_terminal_rows from the same maintenance tick that drives diagnostic_timeline, or gate it behind a counter, and add a (status, created_at) index if it stays on the write path. Deferred: cost is already bounded and self-limiting per fenix's analysis; does not block merge per his PASS verdict." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "performance" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/attention_schedule_store.rs" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-10T21:05:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AZ.4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-10T20:36:42Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FNX-013/AZ4-001> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

# v2: reopened for dispatch, scoped to the minimal mitigation fenix's own
# recommendation allows ("...add a (status, created_at) index if it stays on
# the write path") -- add the index; the write-path-vs-maintenance-tick call
# site itself is not being moved, since that is a larger behavioral change
# fenix already rated as bounded/self-limiting and non-blocking.

